From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] xilinx_dsp: initialize USE_PATTERN_DETECT on generated DSPs

The pattern matcher reads USE_PATTERN_DETECT before deciding whether an
overflow comparator can be packed.  DSP48E1 cells created by addDsp() did not
declare the parameter, so Yosys aborted with "Accessing non existing parameter
\\USE_PATTERN_DETECT" on otherwise ordinary generated arithmetic.

Initialize the parameter to the documented default.  The existing overflow
path still changes it to PATDET when that optimization is selected.

---
 techlibs/xilinx/xilinx_dsp.cc | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/techlibs/xilinx/xilinx_dsp.cc b/techlibs/xilinx/xilinx_dsp.cc
--- a/techlibs/xilinx/xilinx_dsp.cc
+++ b/techlibs/xilinx/xilinx_dsp.cc
@@ -47,6 +47,7 @@ static Cell* addDsp(Module *module) {
 	cell->setParam(ID(PREG), 0);
 	cell->setParam(ID(USE_MULT), Const("NONE"));
 	cell->setParam(ID(USE_SIMD), Const("ONE48"));
+	cell->setParam(ID(USE_PATTERN_DETECT), Const("NO_PATDET"));
 	cell->setParam(ID(USE_DPORT), Const("FALSE"));
 
 	cell->setPort(ID::D, Const(0, 25));
